{"tool_name":"cheripic","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"CHERIPIC","home":"https://github.com/shyamrallapalli/cheripic","license":"MIT","summary":"Computing Homozygosity Enriched Regions In genomes to Prioritize Identification of Candidate variants (CHERIPIC) - tools to pick causative mutation from bulks segregant sequencing.","addition_date":"2019-05-26T09:48:02Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:22Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"version":["1.2.6"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:CHERIPIC","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Shyam Rallapalli","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.com/shyamrallapalli"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/shyamrallapalli/cheripic/wiki/2.-Usage-Instructions"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"De-novo assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0524"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"},{"term":"Variant prioritisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3226"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"CHERIPIC","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s12859-018-2515-5","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2018 The Author(s).Background: Traditional Map based Cloning approaches, used for the identification of desirable alleles, are extremely labour intensive and years can elapse between the mutagenesis and the detection of the polymorphism. High throughput sequencing based Mapping-by-sequencing approach requires an ordered genome assembly and cannot be used with fragmented, un-scaffolded draft genomes, limiting its application to model species and precluding many important organisms. Results: We addressed this gap in resource and presented a computational method and software implementations called CHERIPIC (Computing Homozygosity Enriched Regions In genomes to Prioritise Identification of Candidate variants). We have successfully validated implementation of CHERIPIC using three different types of bulk segregant sequence data from Arabidopsis, maize and barley, respectively. Conclusions: CHERIPIC allows users to rapidly analyse bulk segregant sequence data and we have made it available as a pre-packaged binary with all dependencies for Linux and MacOS and as Galaxy tool.","authors":[{"name":"Chalstrey E."},{"name":"Corredor-Moreno P."},{"name":"MacLean D."},{"name":"Page M."},{"name":"Rallapalli G."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2019-01-07T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Bioinformatics","title":"Rapid fine mapping of causative mutations from sets of unordered, contig-sized fragments of genome sequence"},"pmcid":"PMC6323790","pmid":"30616525","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genetic variation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0199"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CHERIPIC","home":"https://bio.tools/CHERIPIC","license":"MIT","version":"1.2.6","summary":"Computing Homozygosity Enriched Regions In genomes to Prioritize Identification of Candidate variants (CHERIPIC) - tools to pick causative mutation from bulks segregant sequencing.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:cheripic:1.2.6/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"